<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The splash screen's icon. A 288 dp viewport with the art inside the central 192 dp, which
     is what the platform masks a splash icon to; the blue canvas behind it comes from
     windowSplashScreenBackground in themes.xml (values-night/colors.xml).

     Dark mode's copy: BittrColors' dark scheme is white on the blue canvas with the arc in
     the brand yellow (canvasArc), so the mark inverts exactly as LaunchAnimation draws it.

     The art is then scaled to 29.6 dp — LaunchAnimation's LOGO_HEIGHT, the size the mark
     holds through the whole of stage 1. The splash is the animation's first frame, so the
     two have to be the same mark at the same size in the same place: at the drawable's own
     size the mark came up five times too big and snapped down the instant Compose drew,
     which is the "jump" iOS does not have (its launch screen is the lockup at rest). -->
